s ongoing for XEN1120 targeting KV7. Study completion is expected in H2 2026 to support initiating a Phase 2 proof-of-concept study in acute pain.","section":"Business Highlights and Anticipated Milestones","block":46,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-338019","form":"8-K","filedAt":"2026-08-06","reportDate":"2026-08-06","cik":"0001582313","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1582313/000119312526338019/xene-ex99_1.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/db5393d24091fc6f94a7caaba0d162f3636f1d2e95072e3ad37a5741c4b74a4e.bin","sha256":"db5393d24091fc6f94a7caaba0d162f3636f1d2e95072e3ad37a5741c4b74a4e"}},{"id":"cc81f9f6b7cbc55748ffeed4a7137a89ee16e99534919cde03fec62705e37a58","quote":"Beyond azetukalner, Xenon is committed to advancing additional novel treatment approaches to address significant unmet needs in epilepsy.","context":"Early-Stage R&D and Partnered Programs for Epilepsy","section":"Business Highlights and Anticipated Milestones","block":47,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-338019","form":"8-K","filedAt":"2026-08-06","reportDate":"2026-08-06","cik":"0001582313","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1582313/000119312526338019/xene-ex99_1.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/db5393d24091fc6f94a7caaba0d162f3636f1d2e95072e3ad37a5741c4b74a4e.bin","sha256":"db5393d24091fc6f94a7caaba0d162f3636f1d2e95072e3ad37a5741c4b74a4e"}},{"id":"0e255051bf4b6844550ae7b84682bac9fa9183d0fdd782cd9b70a45f9a3027e2","quote":"IND-enabling studies are ongoing for the Company’s oral small molecule NaV1.1 program. Pre-clinical data suggest that targeting NaV1.1 could potentially address the underlying cause and symptoms of Dravet syndrome.","context":"•","section":"Business Highlights and Anticipated Milestones","block":49,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretatio